# Regular expression in Perl format.
# The pattern is the string it is taken off.
# It starts and ends with slash (e.g. "/(your-expression)/"),
# Also it can be specified by the flag option,
# e.g.
# ```
# (`Q.string.regex "/(word)/i").compiled.matches "WORD"
# ```
#
# There are two entry points and one letter between their names.
# `matches` answers whether the whole text matches: the block it finds has
# to start at zero and end at the length of the text, so a pattern that
# covers only part of it answers `false`.
# `match` searches instead: it hands back the first block found anywhere in
# the text, and `next` moves to the one after it.
# ```
# (`Q.string.regex "/[a-z]+/").compiled.matches "1abc"  # false
# (`Q.string.regex "/[a-z]+/").compiled.match "1abc"    # the block "abc"
# ```
#
# Supported flags:
# /d - Enables Unix lines mode.
# /i - Enables case-insensitive matching.
# /x - Permits whitespace and comments in pattern.
# /m - Enables multiline mode.
# /s - Enables dotall mode.
# /u - Enables Unicode-aware case folding.
#
# `compile` reads the expression here: the slashes, the body between them
# and the flag letters after the closing one. A flag that is not one of the
# six above is refused before the flags are spliced in front of the body as
# an inline `(?flags)` group, since a flag section such as `i)|(?:a` would
# otherwise close that group and inject its own alternation into the
# pattern. What comes out is a `pattern` holding the body and the flags.
#
# Two atoms remain, each doing one thing only the engine can do.
# `pattern.checked` tells whether the spliced source compiles, and hands
# the fallback the construct the engine choked on together with the index
# it sits at in the source; the message and the offset into the body the
# caller wrote are made here. `pattern.match.searched` finds the first
# block at or after a position and answers its borders and groups as a
# tuple, empty when there is none; the matched block and the missing one
# are made here from that tuple.

+architect yegor256@gmail.com
+home https://github.com/objectionary/eo
+package string
+rt jvm org.eolang:eo-runtime:0.0.0
+rt node eo2js-runtime:0.0.0
+version 0.0.0
